MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_001: Sleep will not come. What nags at me so?
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_002: I feel restless as a new recruit about to see combat\nfor the first time... Heh.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_003: Hm? Something blocks the street like a sea beast\nwashed ashore.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_004: Some feeling in the pit of my stomach suggests it's\nsomeone I recognize. Don't tell me...
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_005: *snore* Huh? Uh... Oh, hey, boss.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_006: Tobias. Why are you sleeping in the road?
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_007: Huh. Gooood question. I remember having dinner,\nand then...
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_008: I started to nod off, and... *snore*
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_009: You old reprobate. Hey! Wake up.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_010: Hahaha! Lookee here. A sleepy old man and a pretty\nyoung thing.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_011: If you don't wanna die, drop your valuables\nand scram.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_012: Hold your insolent tongue. Know that I am Queen\nTheodora of Saramis, and mind your speech.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_013: Queen, huh? You think we're gonna fall for a pathetic\nbluff like that?
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_014: What kinda queen wanders the streets with an old\nman in the dead of night?
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_015: I concede the situation is odd, but you are a fool\nto doubt my word.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_016: Who you callin' a fool?! Queen or not, you got some\nnerve mouthin' off to us!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_017: Your insolence amuses me.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_018: As you wish, then. I shall cut you both down to pass\nthe time on this sleepless night.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_019: You'll eat those words!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_020: *snore* Huh?!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_021: RAAAH!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_022: Kyaaaah!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_023: Tobias! Were you awake?
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_024: You bastards... Just try to lay a finger on the boss.\nI dare you.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_025: I'll twist the heads off your necks and have 'em for\na midnight snack!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_026: A-aah! This old man's way stronger than he\nlooks. W-we gotta get outta here!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_027: I find myself with no one to point my spear at.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_028: Regardless, that was good work. I am grateful for\nyour intervention, Tobias.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_029: Mmph...
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_030: Tobias! Are you alright? Did they injure you?
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_031: Ugh. My head's splittin'—I drank way, waaay\ntoo much...
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_032: *snore* The night breeze'll fix me right up...
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_C_033: That's all it was? Heh. If only Tobias didn't have\nthese foibles, he would be the perfect attendant.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_00: Where has Tobias gone? I can't find him anywhere.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_01: RAAAGH!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_02: That shout came from outside our camp!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_03: Tobias, report! Are we under attack?
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_04: Wait...what is that absurdly large beast you've\ndragged here?
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_05: Hey, boss! Check out what I caught!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_06: Is this a sand boar? Its size is staggering.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_07: It's larger even than I am. That beast could feed\na hundred soldiers—or more.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_08: You hunted this alone? How did you best it?
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_09: Only way I know how. Popped 'im once right in\nthe snoot.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_10: You felled a charging sand boar with a single punch?!\nYou are fortunate you didn't break your arm.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_11: Yeah, I've been working out. I ain't gonna be lunch\nfor some two-bit beast!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_12: We'll be feasting on sand-boar sandwiches tonight!\nBaw haw haw!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_13: Tobias... When I heard you cry out a moment ago,\nI feared the worst.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_14: I ask again that you do not leave your post.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_15: Hey, don't you worry, boss.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_16: If anything happened to you, I'd dash right over,\nno matter how far away I was!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_17: It was not my life I feared for.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_18: Still feelin' anxious, boss?
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_19: Come on—we'll get some sand-boar steak in you, and\nyou'll feel right as rain.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_20: Baw haw haw!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_B_21: You'll never change...
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_00: Tobias! Answer me, Tobias!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_01: What has he left his post for this time?!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_02: I'm right here, boss!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_03: What?!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_04: Whew. See? I came as soon as you called.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_05: Yes, by dropping from a roof out of nowhere.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_06: The rooftops were not your post. I have been lenient\nwith you this far, but today—
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_07: Sorry, can this wait a sec? I was in the middle of\nsomething up there.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_08: Hmm?
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_09: Uwah...
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_10: Urgh...
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_11: I was in such a hurry, I left the guy I took out up\nthere! But he fell down and saved me the trouble.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_12: An assassin, hmm? Show him how his kind are\nwelcomed in Saramis.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_13: Damn...you...
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_14: I was not aware that you were patrolling even\nthe rooftops.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_15: My rebuke was misguided. Your devotion to duty is\ncommendable.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_16: Nah. I was drinking wine up there and just happened\nto spot him.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_17: Hey, speaking of which, you were sore about my\ndrinking, right? Well, it came in handy this time!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_18: I swear, Tobias...
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_19: What's the matter, boss? You got that look in your\neye again.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_20: Listen, don't worry. Whatever you trust me with,\nI'll handle. Bam!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_21: Baw haw haw haw!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_22: Huh. Incredible.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_23: Whenever you are around, Tobias, all my worries\nstart to feel insignificant.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_24: Aha! A smile! You're smiling!
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_25: Yes, and I daresay it is overdue.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_26: Commander Tobias. Your orders are to continue to\nserve me closely as my personal bodyguard.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_27: I shall brook no argument on this.
MID_SE_Seo_Tob_A_28: You got it, boss!